    "body": "## Motivation\n\n`pr-test-npu.yml`'s `check-changes` filter currently matches **every file in the\nrepository**, so the NPU PR suite runs on every PR — including ones that touch no\nPython at all.\n\n#39110 is the case that surfaced it: a two-file change under\n`experimental/sgl-router/tests/e2e/` pulled in the full A2/A3 NPU fleet\n(`base-a-test-1-npu-a2`, `base-b-test-{1,2,4,8,16}-npu-a3`,\n`base-c-test-acc-{2,16}-npu-a3`), and `pr-test-npu-finish` went red on failures\nin NPU accuracy jobs that the PR could not possibly have caused. That run's own\npaths-filter log lists both router files as matches:\n\n```\nDetected 2 changed files\n##[group]Filter main_package = true\nMatching files:\nexperimental/sgl-router/tests/e2e/chat_completions/test_hicache_storage_tiers.py [added]\nexperimental/sgl-router/tests/e2e/infra/model_pool.py [modified]\n```\n\n### Cause\n\n#39411 rewrote `main_package` from a single extglob into a pattern plus two\nstandalone negations:\n\n```yaml\nmain_package:\n  - \"python/sglang/**/!(*.md)\"\n  - \"!python/sglang/multimodal_gen/**\"\n  - \"!python/sglang/kernels/ops/diffusion/**\"\n```\n\n`dorny/paths-filter` ORs a filter's entries together — `predicate-quantifier`\ndefaults to `some`, so each entry is an independent rule and a file matches the\nfilter if **any** rule matches it. A negated rule matches every path *outside*\nthe path it names, so `!python/sglang/multimodal_gen/**` matches the whole\nrepository minus that one directory. The intended subtraction became a\nrepo-wide union.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSpell the exclusions as extglobs *inside* the patterns, so there are no\nstandalone negated entries. This is the form `_pr-test-check-changes.yml`\nalready uses for the same two directories:\n\n```yaml\nmain_package:\n  - \"python/sglang/!(multimodal_gen|kernels)/**/!(*.md)\"\n  - \"python/sglang/kernels/!(*.md)\"\n  - \"python/sglang/kernels/!(ops)/**/!(*.md)\"\n  - \"python/sglang/kernels/ops/!(*.md)\"\n  - \"python/sglang/kernels/ops/!(diffusion)/**/!(*.md)\"\n```\n\n#39411's intent is preserved: `python/sglang/kernels/ops/diffusion/**` still\nroutes to `multimodal_gen` only, and the `multimodal_gen` filter and the daily\nschedule are untouched. A comment records why the negations cannot come back.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe filter block was parsed straight out of the workflow file and run through\n`picomatch` (same major as the one `dorny/paths-filter@v3` ships) with\n`{dot: true}` and the default `some` quantifier, against all 9176 tracked files.\n\n| | before | after |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| files matching `main_package` | 9176 (100%) | 3840 (41.8%) |\n| non-`python/` files matching `main_package` | 8681 | 0 |\n\nPer-case, with both filters evaluated:\n\n| changed paths | `main_package` | `multimodal_gen` | NPU jobs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| #39110's two router test files | false | false | **skip** |\n| `experimental/sgl-router/src/**` | false | false | **skip** |\n| `rust/**`, `docs/**` | false | false | **skip** |\n| `python/sglang/srt/managers/scheduler.py` | true | true | run |\n| `python/sglang/kernels/ops/moe/topk.py` | true | false | run |\n| `python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/*.cu` | true | false | run |\n| `python/sglang/kernels/ops/diffusion/**` | false | true | run (mm-gen only) |\n| `python/sglang/multimodal_gen/**` | false | true | run (mm-gen only) |\n| `scripts/ci/npu/npu_ci_install_dependency.sh` | true | true | run |\n| `.github/workflows/pr-test-npu.yml` | true | true | run |\n\nAgainst the pre-#39411 filter the only behavioural difference over all tracked\nfiles is the 86 `python/sglang/kernels/ops/diffusion/**` files that #39411\ndeliberately moved out of `main_package`.\n\nNote that this PR touches `pr-test-npu.yml`, which is itself in the filter, so\nthe NPU suite runs on this PR and exercises the new filter end to end.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests) — N/A, CI config only.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations) — N/A.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results — N/A.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Kdf2Dp1apy8yE8vWh3gFAN\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:white_check_mark: [Run #35033361516](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35033361516)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35033361207](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35033361207)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
